Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

When doing a local_install, is it possible to specify option for the local installation? For instance, I want to install the vimcom R package (which is not on CRAN) into my packrat repo. I've used local repos for this by doing the following

mkdir ~/R/packages
cd ~/R/packages
wget http://www.lepem.ufc.br/jaa/vimr/vimcom_1.2-6.tar.gz <http://www.lepem.ufc.br/jaa/vimr/vimcom_1.2-6.tar.gz>
tar -xzvf vimcom_1.2-6.tar.gz

Then in my project with packrat enabled:

packrat::set_opts(local.repos = "~/R/packages")
packrat::install_local("vimcom")

I am assuming this calls install.packages() at some point in install_local with the repos parameter set? In any case, for installing vimcom I need to actually specify the some additional configure options on my Mac OS X (http://www.lepem.ufc.br/jaa/vimcom.html). Normally, I would install this way:

install.packages("vimcom_1.2-6.tar.gz", type = "source", configure.args="--enable-clientserver, --x-includes=/opt/X11/include --x-libraries=/opt/X11/lib", repos = NULL)

Is there a way to set these configuration options with install_local?

Thanks,

Fong

